---SCREEN
=vhset (linlib/visi) preferences setup

  use arrow keys or .:TA... then .:NL... or .:SP... to make menu choice
  
  The .'vhset utility configures the behavior and appearance of all programs
  linked with the linlib library. Customization is performed by reading
  a profile file that is edited here.

  The profile that was found first will fix the compiled default settings:
    .'/etc/vhset/$TERM	(system-wide)
    .'$VHSET/$TERM	(personal)
  
  Do the following to create personal profile:

    $ export VHSET=~/.vhset ; 
    $ mkdir -p $VHSET ; 
    $ touch $VHSET/$TERM

NOTE:
  There is one hidden page called with .'0 key. It allows to change keypad
  activation key and labels for arrow keys which usually are never changed.
---END
